lion-display (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Milestone release v0.7.0 -- the positioning shell (Phase 28):
    where the system puts windows, and the dock it keeps for itself.
    The pure placement engine (ldp-shell::layout): the output's shape
    picks the doctrine -- a portrait output is a phone (every app
    anchors at the usable origin, above the dock; overflow runs under
    it, occluded never destroyed -- the iOS keyboard doctrine), a
    landscape output is a desktop (the classic cascade, caught at the
    usable edge). Placement rides a root's first attach -- the
    position applies with the very commit that maps the surface, so a
    window lands placed, never origin-then-jump -- and live output
    re-arrangements re-place every mapped root immediately (a new
    screen starts a fresh layout, the migration frame itself carries
    the move). The system dock: the phone's home bar -- a frosted bar
    the compositor itself owns (haze plus a row of app pills, ARGB
    ink at a stable identity), rendered above every client layer with
    Phase 27's material language (the frost snapshots the composed
    backdrop, the corner coverage folds at upload -- zero growth of
    the render seam), reserving its thickness out of the usable area,
    and rising from below the edge on a critically damped spring that
    integrates at render cadence from the driver's timestamps
    (bit-reproducible motion; a quiescent compositor holds its last
    integrated offset). The direct-scanout candidacy stays honest
    under chrome (the dock's rect subtracts from the overlay set).
    The doctrine switches: --dock auto|off (CLI default auto; the
    library default stays off so every Phase 26/27 pixel oracle keeps
    byte-exact -- the same contract as the effects tier), the honest
    third startup line ("phone layout, dock 84 px at the bottom"),
    --dock-thickness. 35 new tests (1,804 total): the layout engine
    suite (the carve, the cascade, the clamp, the degenerate outputs),
    the immediate-position damage rule, the shell module suite (the
    ink, the rise's monotone settle, the vacate rule), and the
    end-to-end shell session -- the desktop cascade pixel-exact
    against hand-derived reference math with the frosted dock's haze
    and pills, the phone re-anchor on a portrait swap (the whole
    doctrine re-resolving mid-session), the legacy regression gate,
    the Minimal plain dock, and the whole shell session byte-equal
    under the injected reference GL backend.

