lion-display (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Milestone release v0.5.0 — live output re-arrangement (Phase 26):
    the serving compositor follows the display topology. When a
    hotplug event arrives, the serve loop re-probes the whole
    topology and moves the served pipeline: a monitor swap migrates
    the live pipeline (applied disable, framebuffers released and
    dumb buffers destroyed, a fresh scanout chain allocated, the
    applied enable, the bring-up flip latching the scheduler's
    re-anchored timeline, a full-scene re-render) so the desktop
    survives the swap with every client session intact; the last
    display going away is the honest dark state (pipeline disabled,
    every kernel object released, pending buffer fences flushed,
    frame requests parked with output_off, the protocol still
    serving); the first re-plug relights and the waiting desktop
    paints again. Clients feel the transitions through their output
    objects: revoked (capability_revoked) through the outbox
    wake-point delivery, re-bind for the fresh cascade. A sink
    re-negotiating its mode list (same connector, different modes)
    migrates too -- the pipeline comparison decides, not the status
    diff. Grabs on a dark compositor answer failed(no_output), the
    capture_error vocabulary's second value (spec/capture.toml
    growth through the full ldpc pipeline). 1,727 tests green.

